summary='# MDRouter evidence closure — actual results\n\n'
summary+='**Decision: prioritize an EAB-style analysis; Regular method evidence remains INSUFFICIENT. New formal certification remains NOT_CERTIFIED.**\n\n'
summary+='1. Execution plans: R100 has measured resident E2E savings HR9.08%, Finance20.63%, Industrial34.22% vs FullV, but repairs only1/6,2/5,0/4 originally harmed queries. Mean-risk reduction is distinct from complete harm repair. FullV/BM100/BM25 is the tested minimal routing catalog; BM50 is retained as comparator. R200 remains a static Pareto candidate in HR/Finance and was not trained/served here, so no global optimality claim. Hybrid is dominated on the positive-regret/cost plane in old3domains; mean-quality/cost and3D quality/risk/cost can differ, because signed improvements do not cancel positive harms.\n\n'
summary+='2. New training data: legal PharmaFit81/Dev45 materialized636qrels and504four-plan outcomes,1512timings/504GPUprofiles. All756fixed-capacity/grid/source comparisons retained. At illustrative preset kappa10, Q-regret risk .0221→.0565 and QP .0185→.0512 when n20→81; nativeR² stays negative. This is evidence against a stable benefit in this small development study, not a theorem that more data never help. Do not increase model capacity.\n\n'
summary+='3. Probe: the4-action E2 Dev-selected kappa20 Q/QP risks were.0381/.0125, with matched-static-random conditional paired95% increment intervals[-42.05,+5.14] and[-17.60,+18.11]pp. They do not establish incremental utility. The3-action E4 mask and working points were locked before stream execution; all realized-risk comparisons are reported, not just favorable cells. Query and QP working points can have different risks; direct matched-query-only conservative-mixture streaming was not separately run.\n\n'
summary+='4. Certification: Cal81=81candidatefamilies does not prove81IID; ideal single-policy zero-loss bound.05527 exceeds.05. Ninety IID observations is only an optimistic all-zero single-policy minimum, not a sufficient sample guarantee. Multiple policies/nonzero risk/dependence increase the requirement. New independent task sampling and label-budget approval remain pending; Cal/Eval/oldBL/test/CS reads0.\n\n'
summary+=f'5. Actual serving: {len(stream)}cells, {sum(int(r["request_n"]) for r in stream)}primary arrivals. {len(matched)}/{len(matches)}router-vs-random comparisons have point risk difference<=.005; {len(positive)}have descriptive latency-increment lowerCI>0, {len(negative)}upperCI<0. These are a full grid, not independent significant wins; no simultaneous correction or independent final labels. A/A results and limitations are in E4. In-process resident model/index harness includes buffering, Q/P, queue, planning and actual paths, but excludes network serialization and recreates the worker pool per cell; no complete production/business net claim.\n\n'
summary+='**Next decision:** by10/29 lock a small empirical comparison protocol and the original risk object; by10/30 choose EAB unless genuinely new independent mechanism evidence appears; by11/4 lock reported results. No automatic Cal/Eval release. EAB is conditional on strong general insights, justified heldout descriptive evaluation later if authorized, and a complete public reproducibility package.\n'
